At Fri, 28 Oct 2005 14:10:28 +0200 (METDST),
Clemens Ladisch wrote:
> 
> Takashi Iwai wrote:
> > A. What about names without snd_ like ac97_t?
> >    Should it be "struct ac97" or "struct snd_ac97"?
> 
> The snd_ prefix isn't really necessary in these cases because
> structure tag names are in a seperate namespace and are always local
> to the compilation unit, so they aren't likely to conflict with other
> symbols.
> 
> The only reason to add snd_ would be consistency with other ALSA
> symbols.

Yes, I think "struct ac97" is OK, too.

> BTW: Why didn't ac97_t get a snd_ prefix in the first place?

I don't remember.  No strong reasons, I guess.


Takashi


